# 0.15.0: notes are about what they're indented under. Notes about a screen and its elements are
# listed under the screen, numbered, with a marker on what they're about (after the name for the
# screen itself). Look for: no note inside a screen; the second row starting below the first
# row's notes; the arrows to the second row in lanes under every note; markers on the field's box
# (not its label), on the radios (not the stack's far corner) and clear of the arrow leaving the
# help icon; a note under "Review" with no marker (its button is cut off); and in the measured
# image, the boxes on the drawn notes and markers.
# measured
board "Notes" layout=grid columns=2
  screen phone "Start" height=430 #start
    note "Opens after sign-up" color=blue
    stack row
      heading "Welcome" level=2
      spacer
      icon circle-help #help
        note "Opens the help center"
    input email "Email"
      note "Checked for typos like gmial.com"
    stack gap=10
      radio "Daily" checked
      radio "Weekly"
      note "Daily is the default" color=pink
    button primary "Next" fullWidth #next
  screen phone "Help" height=430 #helpscreen
    navbar "Help" leading=back
    text lines=3
  screen phone "Review" height=430 #review
    text "Check your choices"
    spacer size=600
    button "Below the fold"
      note "Its button is cut off, so it has no marker"
  screen phone "Done" height=430 #done
    heading "Done" level=2
  flow help -> helpscreen "Help"
  flow next -> review
  flow next -> done "Skip review"
